// Source-owned compiler query orchestration.
// The check query follows the Driver's normal load, declaration-comptime,
// body-comptime, and semantic-finalization phases before serialization.
//
// Invocation-memory incremental service. Source of truth: Rust
// QueryService::CompilerQueries and CmdTry::verdict. Sema owns the accepted
// typed body cache; no DriverRecordStore serialization or physical cache.
//
// Ownership and lifetime:
// - One Driver session belongs to one try invocation and survives its edits.
//   It owns canonical document inputs and one opaque Sema session per root.
// - Root results are volatile: prepared source bytes alone do not capture
//   every schema/external/config input. No checked-root memo or hit is claimed.
// - Sema owns all typed body products and their replay. Driver never opens
//   Sema-private fields. Closing the invocation releases its documents and
//   every Sema session; no state leaks into a later try invocation.
//
// Authorized input adapter:
// - The CLI retains Request.prepare_overlays as the one filesystem/authority
//   resolver. check_disk prepares the entry without edits; set_document updates
//   the session's exact canonical-path text; check_text prepares the complete
//   overlay set through the same adapter and enters this existing check flow.
// - Driver receives the actual prepared snapshot and parsed entry packet;
//   it does not reopen display paths, infer a project root, or forward to Rust.
// - Every verdict enters the real checker using the freshly prepared request.
//   Schema/lock/external/comptime/config inputs retain their actual producers,
//   not a source-only root key or a second SourceQuery load.
// - Missing inputs follow ordinary diagnostics. Even unchanged source cannot
//   authorize a root-result hit without the whole actual read closure.
//
// Root query flow:
// - Run the normal load/declaration-comptime/body-comptime/semantic-finalization
//   flow below once with the root's opaque Sema session on the final verdict.
// - Keep registration, policies, plugin interfaces, resolved imports and
//   target/profile facts canonical. This is not a BuildGraph/receipt facade,
//   a second frontend, or two complete checks with inferred reuse counters.
// - Root-result eligibility and Sema-body eligibility are distinct. A volatile
//   root still supplies its opaque Sema session to the FINAL real verdict when
//   that same compile supplies complete actual Sema inputs/frozen epochs.
//   This does not authorize a root hit: fresh global/schema verdict work runs.
//   A body-relevant uncaptured input instead makes that logical BODY query
//   volatile through its real producer; Driver invents no flag or key for it.
//
// Opaque Sema contract (sole implementation editor: SpeedPareto2):
// - Compare the actual graph/stage/values/providers/policies and frozen
//   registration/module views from the same compile. Body-cleared interfaces
//   preserve all headers/defaults/non-body facts; dependency projections strip
//   spans with the canonical quote/escape-aware law, not a guessed serializer.
//   Frozen binding/declaration/source views separately retain their full spans.
// - Capture full relevant/callee source-segment maps and post-summary scope/
//   environment inputs ONCE per request/module epoch, not a scalar name line
//   or an entire graph serialized into each function key. Physical counters/
//   callback addresses/reconstructible indexes are not semantic input.
// - A row retains its own full raw/planned function, owner/generic/memory facts
//   and exact frozen input epoch. Exact owned values decide equality, not a
//   hash alone. No private-body key depends on every other executable body.
// - An entry owns the actual private SemaFunctionResult, WHOLE FnBody and four
//   ordered outputs: diagnostics, calls, comptime requests and name references.
//   Preserve all actual completion/exact-Int/copy/hardware/body-source/compute/
//   failure facts. Do not invent absent publication/pending-ledger arrays.
// - Commit only the accepted complete final owned packet after the main
//   callback retry. wanted_hooks=false alone is insufficient: sticky BOTH-mode
//   host reach and actual foreign HTTP-handler raw-body reads bypass retention.
//   Never retain provisional/withheld/part-borrowed packets. Comptime/embed,
//   volatile and incomplete outcomes use the real logical recompute path.
// - Replay through the SAME ordered append path used by fresh bodies
//   (currently sema_append_function plus its explicit facts loops), preserving
//   parallel result order. Factoring that path belongs to the checker owner;
//   planned helper names are not existing APIs. Re-run all global failure,
//   effect, borrow and other bundle obligations after all body products join.
// - Prepared replay descriptors carry the frozen epoch. Ordered return-view
//   publication invalidates stale descriptors; discarded candidates count no
//   hit and follow canonical checking. Worker results join before mutable apply.
//
// Counters and command cutover:
// - Root hits/recomputes and body hits/recomputes are distinct cumulative
//   observations. Increment a body hit only for an actual accepted replay;
//   increment a body recompute once when the tracked initial logical body
//   query accepts its final outcome, including uncached/bypassed outcomes.
//   Provisional callback attempts do not publish or increment separately;
//   global rechecks/probes are not initial body-cache hits/recomputes.
//   No result-derived counts or synthetic cached claims.
// - Stats use exact Int. clear drops retained rows but preserves cumulative
//   hits/recomputes; clear_measurement resets only the ordered recomputed window.
// - CmdTry takes stats after its baseline check_disk, installs each staged
//   document, calls check_text, and reports checked monotonic deltas of the actual
//   item counters. Decreasing counters are an internal failure, not fake zero.
// - Keep uses the existing SourceTransaction/SemanticOps writer after the
//   checked verdict and current-byte comparison. Default speculation writes
//   no source. Failed checks publish the normal diagnostics, not clean claims.
//
// Acceptance packet:
// - Root verdicts remain volatile. Unchanged and edited inputs exercise actual
//   Sema replay/recomputation while schema/global verdict work always runs.
// - Fresh and replayed packets agree on diagnostics, names, effects, failure,
//   copies, publications and borrow obligations on serial and parallel paths.
// - Exact try human/JSON output, receipt identity and keep/no-keep transaction
//   behavior use real item-counter deltas. Source approval requires the full
//   typed input/replay/caller packet; parser success is not semantic proof.
use {
    jet_sema.[sema_output_legacy_run_contract, sema_output_resolve]
    jet_foundation.[
        Diagnostic,
        SourceFile,
        SymbolKeys,
        module_text,
        source_file_id,
    ]
    jet_sema.[
        SemaCompilerModuleSource,
        SemaComptimeFunctionResult,
        SemaComptimeItemValue,
        SemaGraphResult,
        SemaIncrementalCache,
        sema_incremental_cache_new,
        sema_incremental_cache_clear_measurement,
        sema_incremental_cache_stats,
        SemaRegistrationGraph,
        SemaRegistrationModule,
        SemaRegistrationModuleInput,
        SemaRegistrationPackagePolicy,
        sema_collect_comptime_declarations,
        sema_comptime_graph_apply_values,
        sema_comptime_graph_with_values,
        sema_finalize_graph,
        sema_graph_trail_init,
        sema_graph_trail_undo,
        sema_registration_prepare_graph,
        SemaGraphModuleResult,
        SemaOutputIntent,
    ]
    jet_eval.[
        JetCompilerServicesCheckedFacts,
        JetCompilerServicesCheckedInput,
        JetCompilerServicesParseFacts,
        jet_eval_compiler_services_checked,
    ]
}

// Exactly one requested checked product; failed ingress has no manufactured
// projection or opaque value. Ordinary compiler consumers request the value,
// while the invocation service retains the original checked projection.
JetDriverCompilerCheckProduct: enum {
    CheckedCompilerValue(checked: JetCompilerServicesCheckedFacts)
    RetainedCheckedProjection(projection: JetDriverCheckedProjectionResult)
    Failed
}

JetDriverCompilerCheckInput: struct {
    parsed: JetCompilerServicesParseFacts
    request: JetDriverCompileRequest
    sema_session: SemaIncrementalCache?
    retain_projection: Bool
}

JetDriverCompilerCheckResult: struct {
    product: JetDriverCompilerCheckProduct
    diagnostics: [Diagnostic]
    failed_stage: JetDriverStage?
    complete: Bool
    internal_problem: String?
}

// Invocation-owned documents use paths already resolved by the CLI's retained
// authority adapter. This service never reopens or canonicalizes a display path.
JetDriverCompilerQueryDocument: struct {
    path: String
    source: String
}

JetDriverCompilerQueryStats: struct {
    item_hits: Int
    item_recomputes: Int
    live_items: Int
    live_item_bytes: Int
    recomputed_items: [String]
}

JetDriverCompilerQueries: struct {
    documents: [String:String]
    roots: [String:SemaIncrementalCache]
}

jet_driver_compiler_queries_new: fn() -> JetDriverCompilerQueries Never! {
    JetDriverCompilerQueries{documents: [String:String]{}, roots: [String:SemaIncrementalCache]{}}
}

jet_driver_compiler_queries_set_document: fn(queries: &JetDriverCompilerQueries, path: String, source: String) Never! {
    queries.documents[path] = source
}

jet_driver_compiler_queries_documents: fn(queries: &JetDriverCompilerQueries) -> [JetDriverCompilerQueryDocument] Never! {
    documents := [JetDriverCompilerQueryDocument]{}
    loop (path, source) in queries.documents -> documents.push(JetDriverCompilerQueryDocument{path: path, source: source})
    documents.sort_by(fn(a, b) { a.path <=> b.path })
    documents
}

jet_driver_compiler_queries_stats: fn(queries: &JetDriverCompilerQueries) -> JetDriverCompilerQueryStats {
    total := JetDriverCompilerQueryStats{item_hits: 0, item_recomputes: 0, live_items: 0, live_item_bytes: 0, recomputed_items: [String]{}}
    loop (_, cache) in queries.roots {
        stats: sema_incremental_cache_stats(cache)
        total.item_hits += stats.hits
        total.item_recomputes += stats.recomputes
        total.live_items += stats.live_items
        total.live_item_bytes += stats.live_item_bytes
        total.recomputed_items.extend(stats.recomputed_items)
    }
    total
}

jet_driver_compiler_queries_clear_measurement: fn(queries: &JetDriverCompilerQueries) {
    loop (_, cache) in queries.roots -> sema_incremental_cache_clear_measurement(cache)
}

jet_driver_compiler_queries_check_disk: fn(queries: &JetDriverCompilerQueries, parsed: JetCompilerServicesParseFacts, request: &&JetDriverCompileRequest) -> JetDriverCompilerCheckResult {
    // Disk and text ingress differ only at the existing authorized CLI adapter.
    jet_driver_compiler_queries_check_text(queries, parsed, request)
}

jet_driver_compiler_queries_check_text: fn(queries: &JetDriverCompilerQueries, parsed: JetCompilerServicesParseFacts, request: &&JetDriverCompileRequest) -> JetDriverCompilerCheckResult {
    root: request.authorized_sources.entry_path
    jet_driver_compiler_queries_set_document(queries, root, parsed.source)
    cache: if queries.roots.get(root) == {
        .Val(existing) -> existing
        .None -> {
            created: sema_incremental_cache_new()
            queries.roots[root] = created
            created
        }
    }
    // Root results deliberately remain volatile: every invocation enters the
    // ONE canonical checker, including fresh schema/global/downstream work.
    // Only Sema's exact frozen inputs and actual sticky producers allow replay.
    jet_driver_compiler_check(JetDriverCompilerCheckInput{parsed: parsed, request: request.move(), sema_session: Val(cache), retain_projection: true})
}

jet_driver_compiler_check_failure: fn(load: JetDriverLoadResult, stage: JetDriverStage, problem: String?) -> JetDriverCompilerCheckResult Never! {
    JetDriverCompilerCheckResult{product: .Failed, diagnostics: load.diagnostics, failed_stage: Val(stage), complete: false, internal_problem: problem}
}

jet_driver_compiler_check_package_policies: fn(load: JetDriverLoadResult) -> [SemaRegistrationPackagePolicy] Never! {
    policies := [SemaRegistrationPackagePolicy]{ }
    loop package in load.packages {
        policies.push(SemaRegistrationPackagePolicy{
            package_identity: package.identity,
            authority_allow: package.authority_allow,
            authority_deny: package.authority_deny,
            authority_needs: package.authority_needs,
            runtime_ceiling: package.runtime_ceiling,
            edition: package.edition,
        })
    }
    policies
}
jet_driver_compiler_check_source_bytes: fn(load: JetDriverLoadResult, path: String) -> String? {
    found := String?{None}
    loop file in load.source_files {
        if file.path != path -> next
        if found != None -> return None
        found = Val(file.source)
    }
    found
}

// The loaded text of the entry module's source unit; None unless exactly one
// loaded module is the entry and its unit has exactly one loaded text.
jet_driver_compiler_check_entry_source: fn(load: JetDriverLoadResult) -> String? {
    found := String?{None}
    loop loaded_module in load.modules {
        if loaded_module.module_identity != load.entry_module_identity -> next
        if found != None -> return None
        if loaded_module.source_unit_index < 0 || loaded_module.source_unit_index >= load.source_units.len() -> return None
        found = Val(jet_driver_compiler_check_source_bytes(load, load.source_units[loaded_module.source_unit_index].path) ?? return None)
    }
    found
}

// Path -> position of its first loaded source text, built once per compile so
// each module reads its text without rescanning the file list.
jet_driver_source_file_positions: fn(files: [SourceFile]) -> [String:Int] Never! {
    positions := [String:Int]{}
    loop (index, file) in files {
        if positions.get(file.path) == None -> positions[file.path] = index
    }
    positions
}

// The loaded text of `path`; a module with no loaded text (a compiler-synthetic
// unit) has none.
jet_driver_source_text_at: fn(files: [SourceFile], positions: [String:Int], path: String) -> String Never! {
    if positions.get(path) == .Val(index) -> return files[index].source
    ""
}

jet_driver_compiler_check_module_sources: fn(load: JetDriverLoadResult, canonical: SemaRegistrationModuleInput, canonical_source: String, parsed: JetCompilerServicesParseFacts) -> [SemaCompilerModuleSource]? {
    rows := [SemaCompilerModuleSource]{}
    loop loaded_module in load.modules {
        if loaded_module.source_unit_index < 0 || loaded_module.source_unit_index >= load.source_units.len() -> return None
        unit := load.source_units[loaded_module.source_unit_index]
        source := jet_driver_compiler_check_source_bytes(load, unit.path) ?? return None
        if loaded_module.module_identity == load.entry_module_identity {
            if source != parsed.source -> return None
            if parsed.compiler_source.len() > 0 {
                if parsed.compiler_source.len() != source.len() -> return None
                source = parsed.compiler_source
            }
        }
        duplicate := false
        loop existing in rows {
            if existing.module_identity == loaded_module.module_identity -> duplicate = true
        }
        if duplicate -> return None
        rows.push(SemaCompilerModuleSource{module_identity: loaded_module.module_identity, source: source})
    }
    loop existing in rows {
        if existing.module_identity == canonical.module_identity -> return None
    }
    rows.push(SemaCompilerModuleSource{module_identity: canonical.module_identity, source: canonical_source})
    Val(rows)
}

jet_driver_compiler_check_result: fn(input: JetDriverCompilerCheckInput, registration: &&SemaRegistrationGraph, graph: &&SemaGraphResult, module_sources: [SemaCompilerModuleSource], diagnostics: [Diagnostic]) -> JetDriverCompilerCheckResult {
    graph_complete: graph.complete
    checked := jet_eval_compiler_services_checked(JetCompilerServicesCheckedInput{
        parsed: input.parsed,
        registration: registration.move(),
        graph: graph.move(),
        module_sources: module_sources,
        diagnostics: diagnostics,
    })
    complete := graph_complete && checked.semantic_index_complete
    JetDriverCompilerCheckResult{product: .CheckedCompilerValue{checked: checked}, diagnostics: diagnostics, failed_stage: None, complete: complete, internal_problem: None}
}
jet_driver_compiler_check_diagnostic_packet: fn(
    input: JetDriverCompilerCheckInput,
    registration: &&SemaRegistrationGraph,
    graph: &&SemaGraphResult,
    module_sources: [SemaCompilerModuleSource],
    diagnostics: [Diagnostic],
) -> JetDriverCompilerCheckResult? {
    if graph.modules.len() != registration.modules.len() || !jet_driver_has_errors(diagnostics) -> return None
    if input.retain_projection {
        return Val(JetDriverCompilerCheckResult{product: .Failed, diagnostics: diagnostics, failed_stage: Val(JetDriverStage.Check), complete: false, internal_problem: None})
    }
    Val(jet_driver_compiler_check_result(input, registration, graph, module_sources, diagnostics))
}

jet_driver_compiler_check_parse_only: fn(load: JetDriverLoadResult) -> Bool Never! {
    if load.modules.len() == 0 -> return false
    if load.failed_stage == .Val(stage) -> return stage == JetDriverStage.Parse
    false
}

jet_driver_compiler_check: fn(input: JetDriverCompilerCheckInput) -> JetDriverCompilerCheckResult {
    load := jet_driver_load(input.request)
    parse_only := jet_driver_compiler_check_parse_only(load)
    if (!load.complete || jet_driver_has_errors(load.diagnostics)) && !parse_only -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, load.failed_stage ?? JetDriverStage.Load, None)
    canonical_option := jet_driver_canonical_effect_module(input.request.canonical_effect_source, load.module_table)
    if canonical_option == None -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the embedded compiler-owned Prelude effect source is invalid"))
    canonical := canonical_option ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the embedded compiler-owned Prelude effect source is unavailable"))
    canonical_text: module_text(load.module_table, canonical.module_identity)
    loop unit in load.source_units {
        if jet_driver_module_identity(unit.package_identity, unit.relative_path) == canonical_text || unit.path == canonical.source_file {
            return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Load, Val("an authorized source unit collides with the pinned compiler-owned Prelude effect source"))
        }
    }
    load.generated_source_files.push(SourceFile{id: source_file_id(canonical.source_file), path: canonical.source_file, source: input.request.canonical_effect_source})
    providers := jet_driver_assemble_foreign_providers(input.request.authorized_sources, load)
    if (!load.complete || jet_driver_has_errors(load.diagnostics)) && !parse_only -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Load, None)
    if !jet_driver_foreign_provider_owners_valid(load.modules, providers, load.diagnostics) -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Load, None)
    if !jet_driver_retain_error_prelude_module(load) -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, None)
    module_sources := [SemaCompilerModuleSource]{}
    if {
        input.retain_projection -> {
            // Retained products use the canonical registration/Doc ownership
            // bijection, including ABI catalog units without physical source.
            // Only the actual entry is replaced by the prepared parser's program.
            // The entry is the loaded entry module's own source unit, the row
            // the module-source bijection reads (its loaded path is the
            // unit's, which need not spell the authorized entry path).
            entry_source: jet_driver_compiler_check_entry_source(load) ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the compiler query source is not the exact loaded entry or a loaded module source is missing"))
            if entry_source != input.parsed.source || (input.parsed.compiler_source.len() > 0 && input.parsed.compiler_source.len() != entry_source.len()) {
                return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the compiler query source is not the exact loaded entry or a loaded module source is missing"))
            }
        }
        else -> {
            module_sources = jet_driver_compiler_check_module_sources(load, canonical, input.request.canonical_effect_source, input.parsed) ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the compiler query source is not the exact loaded entry or a loaded module source is missing"))
        }
    }
    setting_refusals: jet_driver_setting_override_diagnostics(load, input.request)
    if setting_refusals.len() > 0 {
        loop diagnostic in setting_refusals -> load.diagnostics.push(diagnostic)
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Load, None)
    }
    target_option := jet_driver_selected_target_machine(input.request, load.diagnostics)
    if target_option == None -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, None)
    target: target_option ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, None)
    // A script's functions take the script variables they name, as a build's
    // do, so the query's facts show the same parameters.
    jet_driver_script_helpers(input.request, load, providers, target)
    registration_inputs_option := jet_driver_registration_module_inputs(load.modules, load.source_units, load.source_files, load.packages, providers, load.diagnostics, input.request.core_sources, false)
    registration_inputs := registration_inputs_option ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Load, None)
    core_seeds := [SemaRegistrationModule]{}
    // A seeded Core module interns into the symbol range it had in the
    // record's check, so the ids its taken rows name are the compile's.
    core_symbols := [SymbolKeys]{}
    if input.request.core_record == .Val(record) {
        core_seeds = jet_driver_core_record_seeds(load.modules, record.module_names.len(), false) ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the Core record can't seed the graph: {err}"))
        if core_seeds.len() > 0 -> core_symbols = record.symbols.copy()
    }
    canonical_identity := canonical.module_identity
    registration_inputs.push(canonical)
    loop index in 0..<registration_inputs.len() {
        if registration_inputs[index].module_identity == load.entry_module_identity {
            registration_inputs[index].program = input.parsed.parsed.program
            jet_driver_script_carry_parameters(load, registration_inputs[index].program)
        }
    }
    registration_count: core_seeds.len() + registration_inputs.len()
    plugin_facts: jet_driver_plugin_facts(input.request, registration_inputs, load.package_identity)
    registration := sema_registration_prepare_graph(
        registration_inputs,
        core_seeds,
        core_symbols,
        load.imports,
        load.package_identity,
        load.entry_module_identity,
        canonical_identity,
        load.module_table.copy(),
        providers,
        target,
        jet_driver_build_facts(load, input.request, target),
        false,
        input.request.compiler_threads,
    )
    // The taken Core modules' comptime values are the record's
    // (jet_driver_core_record_take), as in Pipeline.jet.
    core_values := [SemaComptimeItemValue]{}
    if input.request.core_record == .Val(record) {
        _: jet_driver_core_record_take(registration, record, core_values) ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the Core record can't seed the graph: {err}"))
    }
    if input.retain_projection -> registration.retain_programs = true
    registration.plugin_facts = plugin_facts
    if input.request.mode == JetDriverCompileMode.Test -> registration.test_mode = true
    if input.request.mode == JetDriverCompileMode.Check -> registration.check_tests = true
    output_intent: if input.request.mode == JetDriverCompileMode.Test -> SemaOutputIntent.Test else -> input.request.output_intent
    output_diagnostics: sema_output_resolve(registration, output_intent, input.request.output_address, jet_driver_entry_selection(load) != None)
    loop diagnostic in output_diagnostics -> registration.diagnostics.push(diagnostic)
    if jet_driver_has_errors(output_diagnostics) -> registration.complete = false
    // The legacy `run: fn` contract fails the check without stopping it.
    loop diagnostic in sema_output_legacy_run_contract(registration, output_intent) -> load.diagnostics.push(diagnostic)
    if registration.internal_problem == .Val(problem) -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val(problem))
    // Declaration checking loans the single graph to its stage, then returns it.
    // A registration error or an incomplete module stops the check here; any
    // other declaration error goes on, and the bodies are checked too (Pipeline.jet).
    registration_errors: jet_driver_has_errors(registration.diagnostics)
    stage := sema_collect_comptime_declarations(registration, jet_driver_compiler_check_package_policies(load), input.request.compiler_threads, input.request.trace_sink)
    declared_registration := stage.graph.move()
    stage.graph = None
    registration = declared_registration.move() ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the declaration pass lost its registration graph"))
    if !stage.complete || stage.modules.len() != registration_count || registration_errors {
        jet_driver_comptime_diagnostics_add(load.diagnostics, stage.diagnostics)
        if stage.modules.len() == registration_count {
            trail := sema_graph_trail_init()
            provisional := sema_finalize_graph(registration, trail, stage, [SemaComptimeItemValue]{}, [SemaComptimeFunctionResult]{}, input.request.eval_config.host_hooks, input.request.compiler_threads, None, true, input.request.trace_sink)
            restored := provisional.registration_graph.move()
            provisional.registration_graph = None
            registration = restored.move() ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("semantic finalization lost its registration graph"))
            sema_graph_trail_undo(registration, trail)
            jet_driver_comptime_diagnostics_add(load.diagnostics, provisional.diagnostics)
            packet := jet_driver_compiler_check_diagnostic_packet(input, registration, provisional, module_sources, load.diagnostics)
            if packet == .Val(result) -> return result
        }
        if !jet_driver_has_errors(load.diagnostics) -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val(jet_driver_totality_problem("semantic declaration checking did not return a complete resolved package graph ({stage.modules.len()} of {registration_count} modules checked)", "sema.check", stage.modules, load.module_table)))
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, None)
    }
    // The run starts from the taken Core modules' values, which type their
    // rows first; `core_trail` records those edits, undone with the run's.
    core_trail := sema_graph_trail_init()
    sema_comptime_graph_apply_values(registration, core_values, core_trail)
    // Body/comptime stage callees read the complete load while appending
    // diagnostics, so this existing stage boundary travels beside the load.
    stage_diagnostics := load.diagnostics
    load.diagnostics = [Diagnostic]{}
    // The run owns this same graph and hands it back on every exit.
    declared_modules := stage.modules.move()
    stage.modules = [SemaGraphModuleResult]{}
    declared_facts := stage.graph_facts.move()
    stage.graph_facts = None
    run := jet_driver_run_comptime(
        registration,
        declared_modules,
        declared_facts,
        stage.sources,
        core_values,
        [SemaComptimeFunctionResult]{},
        input.request,
        stage_diagnostics,
    )
    jet_driver_comptime_return_declared(stage, run)
    load.diagnostics = stage_diagnostics
    finished_registration := run.graph.move()
    run.graph = None
    partial_registration := run.partial_graph.move()
    run.partial_graph = None
    registration = jet_driver_comptime_take_registration(finished_registration, partial_registration)
    // The stage's reports reach the result through finalization; a run that
    // stops first carries them itself.
    if run.soft_stop || (!run.complete && run.internal_problem != None) -> jet_driver_comptime_diagnostics_add(load.diagnostics, stage.diagnostics)
    if run.soft_stop -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, None)
    if !run.complete {
        if run.internal_problem == None {
            provisional := sema_finalize_graph(registration, run.trail, stage, run.values, run.functions, input.request.eval_config.host_hooks, input.request.compiler_threads, None, true, input.request.trace_sink)
            restored := provisional.registration_graph.move()
            provisional.registration_graph = None
            registration = restored.move() ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("semantic finalization lost its registration graph"))
            sema_graph_trail_undo(registration, run.trail)
            sema_graph_trail_undo(registration, core_trail)
            jet_driver_comptime_diagnostics_add(load.diagnostics, provisional.diagnostics)
            packet := jet_driver_compiler_check_diagnostic_packet(input, registration, provisional, module_sources, load.diagnostics)
            if packet == .Val(result) -> return result
        }
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, run.internal_problem)
    }
    graph := sema_finalize_graph(registration, run.trail, stage, run.values, run.functions, input.request.eval_config.host_hooks, input.request.compiler_threads, input.sema_session, true, input.request.trace_sink)
    restored := graph.registration_graph.move()
    graph.registration_graph = None
    registration = restored.move() ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("semantic finalization lost its registration graph"))
    sema_graph_trail_undo(registration, run.trail)
    sema_graph_trail_undo(registration, core_trail)
    if graph.modules.len() != registration_count {
        jet_driver_comptime_diagnostics_add(load.diagnostics, graph.diagnostics)
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("semantic finalization did not return every registered module"))
    }
    if jet_driver_core_record_seeded_problem(graph) == .Val(problem) -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val(problem))
    schema_check := jet_driver_check_schema_migrations(input.request, registration, graph, input.retain_projection)
    registration = schema_check.registration.move()
    loop diagnostic in schema_check.diagnostics -> load.diagnostics.push(diagnostic)
    stage_diagnostics = load.diagnostics
    load.diagnostics = [Diagnostic]{}
    body_run := jet_driver_orchestrate_comptime_bodies(
        registration,
        stage,
        graph,
        run.values.move(),
        run.functions.move(),
        jet_driver_empty_compile_trace(),
        load,
        input.request,
        stage_diagnostics,
        None,
    )
    load.diagnostics = stage_diagnostics
    returned_registration := body_run.registration.move()
    body_run.registration = None
    registration = returned_registration.move() ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, Val("comptime body rechecking lost the registration graph"))
    if jet_driver_core_record_seeded_problem(body_run.graph) == .Val(problem) -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, Val(problem))
    if body_run.soft_stop -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, None)
    if !body_run.complete {
        if body_run.internal_problem == None {
            packet := jet_driver_compiler_check_diagnostic_packet(input, registration, body_run.graph.move(), module_sources, load.diagnostics)
            if packet == .Val(result) -> return result
        }
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, body_run.internal_problem)
    }
    graph = body_run.graph.move()
    stage_diagnostics = load.diagnostics
    load.diagnostics = [Diagnostic]{}
    validation := jet_driver_validate_checked_text(
        registration,
        stage,
        graph,
        body_run.values,
        body_run.functions,
        body_run.trace,
        load,
        input.request,
        stage_diagnostics,
    )
    load.diagnostics = stage_diagnostics
    validated_registration := validation.registration.move()
    validation.registration = None
    registration = validated_registration.move() ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, Val("checked text validation lost the registration graph"))
    if validation.soft_stop -> return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, None)
    if !validation.complete {
        if validation.internal_problem == None {
            packet := jet_driver_compiler_check_diagnostic_packet(input, registration, validation.graph.move(), module_sources, load.diagnostics)
            if packet == .Val(result) -> return result
        }
        return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Comptime, validation.internal_problem)
    }
    graph = validation.graph.move()
    if input.retain_projection {
        schema_ingress: schema_check.ingress ?? return jet_driver_compiler_check_failure(load, JetDriverStage.Check, Val("the retained compiler query lost its actual schema input"))
        resolved_registration := sema_comptime_graph_with_values(registration, validation.values)
        projection := jet_driver_project_completed_check(input.request, load, resolved_registration, graph, validation.values, canonical_identity, schema_ingress, validation.trace)
        diagnostics: projection.compile.diagnostics
        failed_stage: projection.compile.failed_stage
        complete: projection.compile.complete
        internal_problem: projection.compile.internal_problem
        return JetDriverCompilerCheckResult{
            product: .RetainedCheckedProjection{projection: projection.move()},
            diagnostics: diagnostics,
            failed_stage: failed_stage,
            complete: complete,
            internal_problem: internal_problem,
        }
    }
    jet_driver_compiler_check_result(input, registration, graph, module_sources, load.diagnostics)
}
